WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.480
<b>Be Strict with Yourself, but Kind to Others</b>

00:00.000 --> 00:02.480
<b>Congrats to the Baseball Team 
on Making Regional Semifinals</b>

00:02.960 --> 00:05.390
Hey, wanna play at my house today?

00:05.390 --> 00:06.420
Huh, are you sure?

00:06.420 --> 00:07.190
Yeah, come on over!

00:07.190 --> 00:08.380
All right!

00:09.340 --> 00:10.180
Huh?

00:10.890 --> 00:12.820
This broom...

00:12.820 --> 00:15.070
How come no one's using it?

00:15.070 --> 00:18.230
Probably because it's the one I always use.

00:18.230 --> 00:21.590
They say the curse spreads to 
whatever the Grim Reaper touches.

00:22.110 --> 00:25.770
You shouldn't touch it either, 
or else they'll say weird things about you.

00:25.770 --> 00:27.200
Wait, what? That's amazing!

00:27.630 --> 00:30.120
It's just like the magic spear Dark Dancer!

00:30.120 --> 00:33.160
Huh? What's that?

00:33.160 --> 00:36.430
It's an amazing weapon that 
curses whoever equips it!

00:37.170 --> 00:39.310
I'm so jealous, Nishimura-san!

00:39.310 --> 00:41.980
You can wield Dark Dancer!

00:41.980 --> 00:44.380
Do you have any other cursed things?

00:44.780 --> 00:46.800
I do...

00:47.300 --> 00:49.740
I hear touching this will curse you, as well.

00:49.740 --> 00:52.860
Wow! Just like the wicked Diabolus Bullet!

00:53.050 --> 00:53.850
This, too.

00:53.850 --> 00:54.920
Wow!

00:54.920 --> 00:57.740
Just like Serpent, the magic sword 
that brings ruin upon its owner!

00:57.950 --> 00:59.130
These, as well.

00:59.130 --> 01:01.920
What?! It works on living things, too?!

01:01.920 --> 01:03.700
You've got a ton of familiars!

01:03.700 --> 01:06.130
You're amazing, Nishimura-san.

01:06.130 --> 01:09.290
You've made so many cursed items.

01:09.290 --> 01:12.490
You look like you're having fun, Takada-kun.

01:12.490 --> 01:14.610
I sure am!

01:14.610 --> 01:17.460
Every day is fun when I'm with you!

01:18.290 --> 01:19.280
Is that right?

01:19.280 --> 01:23.140
In fact, if you weren't here, 
I'd be really bummed.

01:23.140 --> 01:23.780
What?

01:23.780 --> 01:26.440
School wouldn't be any fun at all, y'know?

01:26.440 --> 01:28.340
I need you here, Nishimura-san!

01:28.340 --> 01:30.090
O-Okay.

01:30.090 --> 01:31.290
I really mean it!

01:31.290 --> 01:33.480
O-Okay already!

03:00.030 --> 03:03.990
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

03:04.620 --> 03:10.040
<i>Episode 2 "Lunch Duty and Ghost Photographs and Love Letters"</i>

03:05.030 --> 03:07.450
Curry! Curry!

03:07.450 --> 03:10.120
Curry! Curry!

03:10.120 --> 03:11.350
I can't wait!

03:11.350 --> 03:12.010
Yeah.

03:12.010 --> 03:15.760
Ugh! The Grim Reaper's on lunch duty today?

03:15.760 --> 03:18.490
I bet she'll curse the curry to taste bad.

03:19.680 --> 03:23.760
Does it end up tasting bad 
when you're on lunch duty?

03:23.760 --> 03:26.130
You don't know, new kid?

03:26.130 --> 03:27.450
Isn't it obvious?

03:27.450 --> 03:30.310
I mean, the Grim Reaper wheeled 
that curry over here herself.

03:30.310 --> 03:31.440
Oh, oh!

03:31.810 --> 03:35.130
Kitagawa-kun, can I have 
your share of curry, then?

03:35.130 --> 03:36.100
What?!

03:36.100 --> 03:37.640
Well...

03:38.250 --> 03:41.840
You don't want the curry 
Nishimura-san brought, right?

03:41.840 --> 03:43.520
Because it's cursed.

03:43.520 --> 03:45.220
Th-That's right!

03:45.220 --> 03:48.950
No one wants to eat curry 
served by the Grim Reaper!

03:48.950 --> 03:52.590
I want to eat lots of Nishimura-san's curry!

03:52.910 --> 03:55.050
I'll gobble up the curse, too,

03:55.050 --> 03:58.560
and one day, I'll become
 a Dark Eater for sure!

03:58.560 --> 04:00.610
What's a Dark Eater?

04:00.610 --> 04:04.760
So if you don't want the curry 
that Nishimura-san made,

04:04.760 --> 04:06.750
why can't I have it?

04:07.370 --> 04:09.700
I never said I wouldn't eat it!

04:09.700 --> 04:11.710
You can't have mine! Dummy!

04:11.710 --> 04:12.720
What?!

04:13.040 --> 04:15.510
I thought he was scared of the curse...

04:15.510 --> 04:18.650
Kitagawa-kun sure is a weird one.

04:22.260 --> 04:24.590
T-Takada-kun.

04:25.170 --> 04:28.090
Um... thank you.

04:28.090 --> 04:29.700
Huh? For what?

04:30.120 --> 04:32.120
<b>Milk</b>

04:32.580 --> 04:34.900
Who's in for rock-paper-scissors
 for the last milk?

04:34.900 --> 04:36.400
Me!

04:35.100 --> 04:36.650
Me!

04:36.650 --> 04:39.000
Heck yeah! I'm gonna win for sure!

04:39.000 --> 04:40.500
Looks like my time has come.

04:41.920 --> 04:43.580
Oh, man! Let's hurry!

04:43.580 --> 04:47.040
Wait. I don't need two cartons of milk.

04:47.050 --> 04:50.720
This Month's Goal

04:47.050 --> 04:50.720
<b>Let's all get along!{bottom black}</b>

04:47.480 --> 04:49.540
All righty. I'm going for it! I won't lose!

04:49.540 --> 04:50.730
Today's the day!

04:54.930 --> 04:57.940
I was so close in milk 
rock-paper-scissors...

04:57.940 --> 05:01.900
T-Takada-kun, do you want my milk?

05:01.900 --> 05:02.950
I can have it?!

05:02.950 --> 05:03.910
Thanks!

05:03.900 --> 05:06.910
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

05:07.820 --> 05:09.160
Nishimura-san!

05:09.860 --> 05:12.030
Wanna take photos together?

05:12.030 --> 05:16.030
S-Sure, but that came out of nowhere.

05:17.360 --> 05:23.630
The kids in class were talking about how 
a ghost shows up in pictures with you.

05:23.630 --> 05:29.180
<i>I'm pretty sure </i>I'm<i> the ghost
 they're talking about...</i>

05:29.180 --> 05:30.920
Hey, look.

05:30.920 --> 05:33.940
Isn't there a ghost in this photo?

05:33.940 --> 05:36.390
I think that's Nishimura-san.

05:37.200 --> 05:39.200
She <i>does</i> look like one!

05:44.810 --> 05:46.410
I'm gonna take it!

05:46.780 --> 05:47.890
I'm gonna take it!

05:47.890 --> 05:49.010
O-Okay.

05:57.090 --> 06:00.360
I don't see any ghosts here.

06:00.360 --> 06:03.890
I'm pretty sure it's there. 
Right next to you.

06:03.890 --> 06:05.000
What?!

06:05.000 --> 06:06.700
A-Amazing!

06:06.700 --> 06:10.400
Does this mean you can see ghosts and stuff?!

06:10.680 --> 06:12.240
N-No, I can't.

06:12.240 --> 06:13.460
That's not what I meant.

06:13.460 --> 06:14.570
Hey, Takada!

06:15.470 --> 06:18.060
You don't get it at all.

06:18.730 --> 06:20.790
Hino-kun?!

06:20.790 --> 06:24.790
You think a real ghost's
 gonna show up for someone

06:24.790 --> 06:27.810
having so much fun taking ghost pictures?

06:28.120 --> 06:29.400
He's got a point.

06:29.400 --> 06:31.490
Huh? You think so?

06:31.490 --> 06:35.620
Hino-kun gets real invested 
in the supernatural and tank tops.

06:36.900 --> 06:39.200
That's a broad range of interests...

06:40.040 --> 06:42.760
I'll control the shutter this time.

06:42.760 --> 06:45.590
So no looking like you're having fun.

06:45.590 --> 06:47.830
O-Okay.

06:48.190 --> 06:51.110
We can't look like 
we're having any fun at all.

06:51.730 --> 06:53.000
Absolutely none!

06:53.000 --> 06:54.740
R-Right.

06:54.740 --> 06:56.040
You ready?

06:56.430 --> 06:57.980
Here we go!

07:01.540 --> 07:03.520
Hey, Takada!

07:03.870 --> 07:05.530
Takada-kun...

07:05.530 --> 07:08.290
You look like you're having 
the time of your life.

07:11.300 --> 07:13.160
That's weird.

07:13.160 --> 07:15.150
I put on my serious face.

07:15.150 --> 07:17.880
Maybe it's 'cause I'm with Nishimura-san.

07:18.460 --> 07:23.340
Just being with her puts a smile on my face.

07:24.140 --> 07:25.400
What's wrong?

07:26.060 --> 07:28.470
It... It's nothing.

07:29.420 --> 07:32.300
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

07:33.350 --> 07:34.800
I'm home!

07:37.670 --> 07:41.770
<i>My little brother in fifth grade
 brought home a girl.</i>

07:42.640 --> 07:46.890
Um... Who's this, Taiyou?

07:46.890 --> 07:49.330
How do you know each other? Well?

07:49.330 --> 07:51.730
This is my classmate, Nishimura-san.

07:51.730 --> 07:54.950
I'm proud to call her my closest friend!

07:54.950 --> 07:56.420
E-Er...

07:56.420 --> 07:58.490
When you say you're close, do you mean...

07:58.730 --> 08:02.170
W-We're just normal friends!

08:02.490 --> 08:05.110
<i>Oh my, look at her turning red!</i>

08:05.110 --> 08:06.250
<i>How adorable!</i>

08:06.600 --> 08:10.350
Nishimura-san, you can call me Yukiko.

08:10.350 --> 08:12.220
Take good care of Taiyou!

08:12.220 --> 08:15.140
We're really just normal friends!

08:15.140 --> 08:17.300
<i>There she goes blushing again!</i>

08:18.120 --> 08:20.780
C'mon, let's go and play video games!

08:20.780 --> 08:22.340
S-Sure.

08:22.340 --> 08:25.100
My, my, look at you 
taking her hand like that.

08:25.100 --> 08:27.280
Pretty smooth, Taiyou.

08:30.590 --> 08:32.720
It's amazing, Onee-chan!

08:32.720 --> 08:37.020
If you hold hands with Nishimura-san, 
it really feels like you're cursed!

08:38.280 --> 08:41.880
How could you say that to a girl?!

08:41.880 --> 08:42.530
What?!

08:42.530 --> 08:46.620
But it's true! I can feel so 
much power coming from her!

08:47.180 --> 08:51.740
I'm pretty sure that's all 
in your head, Takada-kun.

08:53.100 --> 08:54.920
T-Taiyou!

08:54.920 --> 08:58.300
Look! Nishimura-san's mad because 
you said something weird!

08:58.300 --> 09:01.060
Huh? Why? What'd I say?

08:59.920 --> 09:01.760
Take it back! Go on!

09:02.060 --> 09:03.720
Whaaat?!

09:03.720 --> 09:05.950
O-Onee-chan!

09:03.950 --> 09:07.310
Th-This is my normal face.

09:07.770 --> 09:09.740
Take it back already.

09:10.720 --> 09:15.870
When I hold hands with Nishimura-san, 
I get really happy!

09:15.870 --> 09:17.620
T-Taiyou!

09:18.970 --> 09:21.580
Th-Thanks.

09:21.920 --> 09:25.690
<i>Sh-She's beet red!</i>

09:25.690 --> 09:28.240
<i>How cute can you get? What an angel!</i>

09:28.580 --> 09:30.840
HP 
MP 
Speed 
Defense
 Recovery

09:28.580 --> 09:30.840
Are you sure?

09:28.580 --> 09:30.840
Yes
No

09:28.580 --> 09:30.840
Back

09:29.530 --> 09:30.840
Hey, hey!

09:30.840 --> 09:33.350
This character looks like you.

09:33.350 --> 09:35.670
Huh? Y-You think?

09:35.670 --> 09:36.730
Yeah!

09:36.730 --> 09:38.060
<i>Taiyou...</i>

09:38.060 --> 09:43.330
<i>Your big sister... really loves 
watching scenes like this play out.</i>

09:43.810 --> 09:46.810
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

09:46.810 --> 09:48.810
Theme
Your favorite word

09:48.800 --> 09:50.380
Okay, get started!

09:48.810 --> 09:52.480
Theme
Your favorite word

09:51.020 --> 09:52.470
What?

09:52.940 --> 09:54.730
I really have no idea.

09:54.730 --> 09:55.760
Hi-yah!

09:54.730 --> 09:56.000
What should I pick?

09:55.760 --> 09:58.090
Oh, not half bad!

09:58.090 --> 09:59.720
And when you let your guard down...

09:58.830 --> 10:00.370
Not happening!

10:00.370 --> 10:01.520
Get him, get him!

10:01.520 --> 10:03.800
I can't decide at all.

10:02.000 --> 10:04.750
I feel like I'm gonna get this on my clothes.

10:03.790 --> 10:05.090
Same.

10:04.260 --> 10:06.380
Don't get your sleeves dirty.

10:04.770 --> 10:06.380
How should I write this?

10:08.810 --> 10:10.670
We're supposed to pick our favorite word.

10:10.670 --> 10:12.340
What're you gonna write?

10:12.340 --> 10:16.020
Hmm, I think I'll go with "tank top."

10:16.020 --> 10:16.790
Oh!

10:17.290 --> 10:18.960
What about you?

10:18.960 --> 10:21.590
I'm gonna use you, Nishimura-san!

10:18.960 --> 10:21.590
C'mon, Kitagawa, Tanaka, Yamamoto.

10:21.590 --> 10:23.170
Get to work already!

10:21.590 --> 10:24.460
Would "Grim Reaper" look 
the coolest, you think?

10:23.170 --> 10:24.460
We're sorry...

10:24.460 --> 10:27.970
Wh-Why pick me?

10:27.970 --> 10:31.280
Well, the awesome factor...

10:31.280 --> 10:33.710
And you could say I'm infatuated.

10:33.710 --> 10:36.480
You mean with my nickname, right?

10:38.860 --> 10:42.890
I-I really don't think you 
should write "Grim Reaper."

10:42.890 --> 10:45.100
Everyone in class will tease you.

10:45.100 --> 10:46.780
What?!

10:46.780 --> 10:49.100
Then what are you gonna write?

10:49.100 --> 10:50.530
What's your favorite word?

10:50.790 --> 10:51.460
Huh?

10:53.180 --> 11:00.000
I... don't like dark and gloomy words 
because they remind me of myself.

11:00.000 --> 11:03.500
So I like words that are the total opposite.

11:03.500 --> 11:06.690
Like "hikari" (light) or "taiyou" (sun)...

11:07.300 --> 11:08.390
Oh.

11:08.390 --> 11:10.640
<b>Takada Taiyou</b>

11:08.800 --> 11:10.640
Ah... Er...

11:10.640 --> 11:13.160
I, uh... U-Um...

11:13.160 --> 11:14.840
You like sunshine?

11:14.840 --> 11:15.390
Huh?

11:15.650 --> 11:18.540
Yeah, that's it! I love sunshine!

11:18.540 --> 11:20.390
I meant <i>that</i> "taiyou"!

11:20.390 --> 11:22.510
I love sunshine, too!

11:22.510 --> 11:24.400
It gets a little too hot in summer, though.

11:24.400 --> 11:26.300
I-I agree.

11:26.300 --> 11:29.120
It's real bad, you two. Help me out.

11:29.120 --> 11:30.230
What's the matter?

11:30.230 --> 11:33.370
I don't know how to write "tank top" in kanji.

11:34.430 --> 11:36.530
Can't you just use katakana?

11:37.000 --> 11:42.010
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

11:37.000 --> 11:42.010
Tanku Toppu

11:37.000 --> 11:42.010
DARK DANCER

11:37.000 --> 11:42.010
Sunshine

11:37.000 --> 11:42.010
Love

11:43.520 --> 11:44.260
What?

11:44.260 --> 11:46.010
Takada-kun caught a cold?

11:46.010 --> 11:50.020
Yeah. He said he's too 
sick to hang out today.

11:50.020 --> 11:53.350
I see. I hope he's okay.

11:53.350 --> 11:57.170
I've told him so many times 
to keep his shoulders warm.

11:57.170 --> 12:00.080
Aren't you the one who
 should be worried about that?

12:00.080 --> 12:04.270
Anyway, let's go to Takada's 
place and pay him a visit.

12:04.270 --> 12:07.710
Huh? I-Is it okay to visit 
without any notice?

12:07.710 --> 12:10.290
What if we end up disturbing him instead?

12:11.150 --> 12:16.110
If you go visit him, 
I'm sure Takada would be thrilled.

12:16.820 --> 12:18.930
Y-You think so?

12:20.150 --> 12:22.640
Well, duh. We're talking about Takada here.

12:22.910 --> 12:27.380
I'll be with you, so he'll be over the moon.

12:28.330 --> 12:30.530
H-Hino-kun!

12:31.190 --> 12:34.090
Y-Yeah, you're right...

12:34.090 --> 12:35.920
You're best friends, after all.

12:35.920 --> 12:36.820
Smirk.

12:37.880 --> 12:41.040
<i>A shockingly embarrassing 
misunderstanding on my part!</i>

12:44.830 --> 12:46.280
Coming!

12:46.280 --> 12:48.250
Oh? What's this?

12:48.250 --> 12:50.320
H-Hello there.

12:50.320 --> 12:51.700
We're visiting the patient.

12:51.700 --> 12:55.160
S-Sorry. We can leave if we're being a bother.

12:55.370 --> 12:57.570
You're not bothering me at all!

12:57.570 --> 13:00.180
I'm really glad you two came over.

13:02.580 --> 13:03.630
<i>Told ya.</i>

13:03.630 --> 13:05.550
Hino-kun!

13:05.880 --> 13:08.890
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

13:13.430 --> 13:15.350
<b>Nanba</b>

13:13.430 --> 13:15.350
<b>Nishimura</b>

13:16.770 --> 13:19.560
N-N-Nishimura-san!

13:21.540 --> 13:26.700
N-Nishimura-san, wait, is that...

13:26.700 --> 13:28.590
a love letter?!

13:29.320 --> 13:31.750
Amazing, Nishimura-san!

13:31.750 --> 13:33.410
I mean, you <i>are</i> the coolest!

13:34.700 --> 13:37.170
This is just a prank.

13:37.170 --> 13:39.170
Or a stupid punishment game.

13:39.170 --> 13:43.130
You think someone wrote you 
a fake love letter as punishment?

13:43.130 --> 13:44.070
Yeah.

13:44.070 --> 13:47.230
Fake love letters 
to the Grim Reaper to tease her.

13:47.230 --> 13:49.630
The usual nonsense about curses.

13:49.630 --> 13:51.340
I see!

13:52.160 --> 13:55.500
Takada-kun, you don't really get it, do you?

13:56.030 --> 13:59.510
Does this mean I can write 
you a love letter, as well?

13:59.510 --> 14:00.540
Why?!

14:00.390 --> 14:01.870
Let's go.

14:00.540 --> 14:02.080
You're cursed, right?

14:02.080 --> 14:04.510
I want you to curse me!

14:04.510 --> 14:07.920
Sometimes, it feels like that's 
all you hear, Takada-kun.

14:07.920 --> 14:11.230
I'll write down tons of good things about you!

14:11.230 --> 14:13.150
T-Tons?

14:13.150 --> 14:15.580
A-Are there really that many?

14:15.580 --> 14:17.870
Sure there are! I can name a bunch!

14:17.870 --> 14:20.870
There's your cool gaze, for one.

14:21.490 --> 14:26.340
Oh, and I can't leave out that 
you were willing to be my friend.

14:26.640 --> 14:30.090
I... should be the one saying that.

14:31.120 --> 14:32.220
Ah!

14:32.220 --> 14:33.720
What do I do, Nishimura-san?!

14:33.720 --> 14:35.180
Wh-What is it?

14:35.490 --> 14:39.730
I-I don't think I can fit it all in a letter!

14:39.730 --> 14:42.310
There are so many things I like about you!

14:43.200 --> 14:45.950
Once I put it into words, 
can I say it out loud instead?

14:46.440 --> 14:47.600
Out loud?!

14:59.080 --> 15:01.270
<i>H-He's really gonna say it.</i>

15:03.150 --> 15:04.870
I've got it all ready!

15:04.870 --> 15:05.620
What?!

15:16.650 --> 15:20.160
By the way, how was this a punishment?

15:20.570 --> 15:24.420
I don't think it really applies to you.

15:24.420 --> 15:25.930
I mean, you're unstoppable.

15:25.930 --> 15:28.160
I'm unstoppable? That rules!

15:28.160 --> 15:31.520
Does that mean I possess 
Grim Reaper powers now?!

15:32.350 --> 15:34.290
You really are unstoppable...

15:34.740 --> 15:37.750
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

15:48.070 --> 15:49.680
Nishimura-san!

15:50.220 --> 15:51.280
Ah.

15:51.280 --> 15:53.540
Hello there, Yukiko-san.

15:53.540 --> 15:55.480
Been doing some shopping there?

15:55.480 --> 15:57.180
At a bookstore, by the look of it.

15:57.180 --> 16:00.720
Y-Yes, there were some 
books I wanted to get.

16:00.720 --> 16:02.270
Do you like reading?

16:02.270 --> 16:03.750
As much as anyone else.

16:03.750 --> 16:05.470
I see, I see.

16:05.470 --> 16:07.890
I know! Are you free to come over?

16:07.890 --> 16:08.890
Huh?

16:09.120 --> 16:11.780
My brother's out for his lessons, though.

16:11.780 --> 16:12.710
What?

16:23.950 --> 16:26.320
U-Um...

16:31.060 --> 16:34.250
Mm-hmm, you look adorbs in that.

16:34.250 --> 16:37.830
I-I can't accept these clothes.

16:37.830 --> 16:40.990
It's fine! They're just my old hand-me-downs.

16:41.320 --> 16:44.800
If you won't take them, I'll just make 
my little brother wear 'em instead.

16:43.290 --> 16:44.420
Whoo!

16:44.800 --> 16:46.980
T-Takada-kun, in these?

16:46.980 --> 16:48.750
They look so good on you!

16:48.750 --> 16:49.700
You're so cute!

16:49.700 --> 16:50.980
This angle's great, too!

16:50.980 --> 16:52.480
C'mon, give me a smile!

16:52.480 --> 16:53.650
You look adorable!

16:54.670 --> 16:58.780
But if I wear clothes that are too cutesy,

16:58.780 --> 17:01.400
everyone in my class will laugh at me.

17:01.400 --> 17:04.490
Why's that? You look great in them.

17:04.490 --> 17:06.470
I-I mean...

17:06.860 --> 17:09.930
everyone calls me the Grim Reaper.

17:09.930 --> 17:11.170
And, well...

17:11.680 --> 17:13.770
That's a cool nickname.

17:13.770 --> 17:17.130
But what's it got to do with how you dress?

17:18.750 --> 17:21.860
You should wear what you want 
instead of worrying about it.

17:21.860 --> 17:24.290
And if they're mean about it,

17:24.290 --> 17:26.990
you can just have my brother save the day.

17:28.270 --> 17:32.340
But then I'd be causing 
trouble for Takada-kun...

17:32.340 --> 17:36.030
It's fine. He's the one 
who enjoys it the most.

17:36.030 --> 17:40.740
Besides, Taiyou never shuts up 
about you even at home.

17:40.740 --> 17:42.460
Wha... Wha...

17:42.460 --> 17:46.970
And whenever he's talking 
about you, he looks so happy.

17:46.970 --> 17:48.320
Honest truth.

17:48.860 --> 17:52.090
Th-Thank you so much!

17:53.900 --> 17:56.490
You really are cute in that.

17:56.490 --> 17:58.840
I want to show Taiyou as soon as possible.

18:01.840 --> 18:03.610
You're just the cutest thing.

18:06.100 --> 18:09.100
My <b>Clueless</b> First Friend

18:12.090 --> 18:13.810
A bad luck aura?

18:13.810 --> 18:16.760
It's another one of Nishimura's curses.

18:16.760 --> 18:20.070
You get bad luck when 
you hang out with the Grim Reaper.

18:20.070 --> 18:23.790
A bad luck aura... That sounds so cool.

18:23.790 --> 18:28.700
That reminds me! Hino-kun said he's 
into superstitions like that.

18:28.700 --> 18:32.230
Does that mean you're into tank tops, too?

18:32.230 --> 18:33.510
Where'd that come from?!

18:33.510 --> 18:38.390
Whatever! You keep hanging out with that
 creeper Grim Reaper, and you're in for it!

18:38.390 --> 18:40.470
Because of Nishimura-san's curse?

18:40.470 --> 18:41.700
That's right!

18:41.700 --> 18:43.960
So come join us instead.

18:43.960 --> 18:45.840
Leave the Grim Reaper in the dust.

18:46.950 --> 18:49.760
But being with Nishimura-san is fun.

18:49.760 --> 18:53.080
Only because you haven't noticed yet.

18:53.080 --> 18:57.070
Your luck is slowly getting worse
 because of her curse.

18:57.070 --> 18:58.740
That's how the aura works.

18:58.740 --> 19:00.510
Wow...

19:02.500 --> 19:08.760
This means Nishimura-san is making me
so happy that it's offsetting my bad luck.

19:09.160 --> 19:12.250
I-I didn't say anything like that, new kid!

19:12.250 --> 19:17.140
How else can you explain why I have 
so much fun with Nishimura-san?

19:17.140 --> 19:19.670
I'd better thank her!

19:19.670 --> 19:20.180
See ya!

19:21.950 --> 19:24.480
Hey, what do you think, Kitagawa-kun?

19:24.480 --> 19:27.390
Don't ask me! Scram already!

19:29.910 --> 19:32.160
Hello. Nishimura speaking.

19:32.700 --> 19:36.470
Yes. Yes. From her class?

19:37.440 --> 19:38.860
Akane!

19:39.230 --> 19:41.350
T-Takada-kun?

19:41.350 --> 19:43.980
Why are you calling so late at night?

19:43.980 --> 19:46.780
<i>There's something I need to tell you.</i>

19:46.780 --> 19:49.180
Huh? What is it?

19:49.180 --> 19:50.650
Nishimura-san...

19:50.650 --> 19:53.700
<i>Thanks for always making me so happy!</i>

19:53.700 --> 19:54.480
What?!

19:55.000 --> 19:58.230
Next time, I'll be the 
one to make you happy!

19:58.230 --> 20:00.480
<i>Wh-What's this all about?!</i>

20:02.560 --> 20:04.510
<i>Well, see you tomorrow!</i>

20:09.130 --> 20:11.990
That was so much fun, we ended up 
talking for two whole hours.

20:11.990 --> 20:14.530
It sure was embarrassing
 to say thank you like that.

20:14.530 --> 20:17.170
That's not the part that 
should embarrass you.

21:48.470 --> 21:50.160
Didn't I tell you to keep 
your shoulders warm?

21:50.160 --> 21:51.800
Ah, I'm all better now!

21:51.800 --> 21:52.750
Really?

21:55.160 --> 21:58.370
Whoa! It's so white!

21:58.370 --> 21:59.790
Good morning.

21:59.790 --> 22:02.810
You're not Nishimura-san!
Now you're Whitemura-san!

22:02.810 --> 22:04.830
Gee wowzers!

22:04.830 --> 22:08.390
I-I thought white would 
be a nice change of pace.

22:09.070 --> 22:12.910
I got a lot of clothes from your big sister.

22:13.930 --> 22:15.220
Wow.

22:15.530 --> 22:18.210
Does white look weird on me?

22:18.210 --> 22:20.700
Not at all! You wear it well!

22:20.700 --> 22:22.990
White looks really good on you!

22:23.340 --> 22:25.630
Th-Thanks.

22:25.630 --> 22:28.800
Sorry, I can't tell the difference.

22:28.800 --> 22:30.610
It's all sleeves to me.

22:33.620 --> 22:34.990
What's so funny?

22:34.990 --> 22:40.990
Just that Nishimura-san's 
trying pretty hard for once.

22:40.990 --> 22:45.510
Even though she's still the Grim Reaper,
 no matter how cute her clothes.

22:46.500 --> 22:52.010
Ooh, you mean she's still strong 
even though she looks this cute?

22:52.010 --> 22:54.260
That's way too awesome!

22:54.260 --> 22:56.980
H-How'd you come to that conclusion?

22:56.980 --> 22:59.710
Well, based on what you said,

22:59.710 --> 23:04.020
Nishimura-san's Grim Reaper powers don't wane,
 no matter what she's wearing.

23:04.020 --> 23:05.680
That rocks!

23:05.680 --> 23:08.120
Nishimura-san really <i>is</i> the coolest.

23:08.120 --> 23:10.040
I'm impressed, Kasahara-san.

23:10.570 --> 23:12.270
What do you mean?

23:12.270 --> 23:18.000
When I saw Nishimura-san just now, 
all I could think is "Wow, she's cute!"

23:18.700 --> 23:19.550
What?

23:20.410 --> 23:24.210
Oh! I don't mean that black 
doesn't look good on you!

23:24.210 --> 23:29.020
It's way high on the coolness scale,
and white ranks on the cuteness scale.

23:28.170 --> 23:30.440
I-I get it already!

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next time...</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Summer Vacation Begins</b>

23:34.970 --> 23:39.970
<b>Please adopt me</b>
